  "tweets": [
    {
      "figspec": "fig-01",
      "figures": [
        "fig-01"
      ],
      "n": 1,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "citations": [],
          "i": 1,
          "narrative": true,
          "text": "Every cable that runs into a sealed machine drags grit in with it, and the usual cure is a shutdown and a pair of tweezers."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            "M7"
          ],
          "i": 2,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "This filing claims a way to make the grit stay outside."
        }
      ],
      "slot": "hook"
    },
    {
      "figspec": "fig-02",
      "figures": [
        "fig-02"
      ],
      "n": 2,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "citations": [
            "M1"
          ],
          "i": 1,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "The housing does the ordinary thing here: it defines a guide channel that carries the cable through the wall of the enclosure."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            "M2"
          ],
          "i": 2,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "What the claim adds sits at the mouth of that channel, a wiper collar that the cable has to pass through on its way in."
        }
      ],
      "slot": "stop"
    },
    {
      "figspec": "fig-03",
      "figures": [
        "fig-03"
      ],
      "n": 3,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "citations": [
            "M2"
          ],
          "i": 1,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "The collar is not a seal in the usual sense, because it never grips the cable and never has to be squeezed tight against it."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            "M7"
          ],
          "i": 2,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "It stands proud of the mouth instead, so the grit riding in on the cable is wiped off outside the wall rather than inside the box."
        }
      ],
      "slot": "stop"
    },
    {
      "figspec": "fig-03",
      "figures": [
        "fig-03"
      ],
      "n": 4,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "citations": [
            "M3"
          ],
          "i": 1,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "Here is the admission tucked into the dependent claim: the collar is an elastomeric sleeve, which is to say a part that is meant to wear."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            "M9"
          ],
          "i": 2,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "The drawing puts that sleeve on the outer face, where a hand can reach it without opening the enclosure at all."
        }
      ],
      "slot": "pivot"
    },
    {
      "figspec": "fig-01",
      "figures": [
        "fig-01"
      ],
      "n": 5,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "citations": [],
          "i": 1,
          "narrative": true,
          "text": "So the invention is smaller than the problem it answers, and more candid about itself than most."
        },
        {
          "citations": [
            "M8"
          ],
          "i": 2,
          "narrative": false,
          "text": "It buys back the maintenance stop by admitting up front that one soft part is there to be replaced."
        }
      ],
      "slot": "landing"
    },
